rted metrics. This is non-negotiable for a quantitative empirical paper with small effect sizes.\n2. **Extend to 5–10 generations** to make meaningful claims about iterative processes.\n3. **Add Full-FT at 1.5B** (and ideally 7B) to validate the LoRA/Full-FT divergence finding.\n4. **Expand related work** to 25+ references covering SPIN, STaR, ReST, ReST-EM, best-of-N, Gao et al. reward overoptimization, diversity metrics literature. Position the paper clearly against these.\n5. **Reframe the contribution:** Either (a) provide theoretical analysis of why prompt diversity + reward saturation prevents collapse (making it a contribution about understanding rather than observation), or (b) propose and validate a mitigation for format collapse.\n6. **Add K=16 random baseline and base→Gen 0 measurement.**\n7. **Tighten the title and claims** to match actual evidence scope (\"3 generations of best-of-K on 0.6B/1.5B models\" rather than \"Systematic\" study of \"Resilience\")."}],"totalDurationMs":42610,"totalTokens":18191,"totalToolUseCount":0,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8226,"cache_read_input_tokens":8251,"output_tokens":1712,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8226},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1712,"cache_read_input_tokens":8251,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8226,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}}}
